WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.442
The block loads the seven keep flags into

00:00:03.442 --> 00:00:06.016
shared memory. Lane six begins with one,

00:00:06.016 --> 00:00:08.222
and the extra slot contains zero.

00:00:12.722 --> 00:00:15.427
Lane six reads from distances one, two,

00:00:15.427 --> 00:00:17.745
and four over successive stages. What

00:00:17.745 --> 00:00:19.677
running total will it produce?

00:00:28.177 --> 00:00:30.650
Each stage uses barriers to separate reads

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.122
from writes, so every lane reads values

00:00:33.122 --> 00:00:34.535
from the previous stage.

00:00:39.035 --> 00:00:42.066
The inclusive total at index six is four.

00:00:42.066 --> 00:00:44.340
Since destinations start at zero, the

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.992
final kept item goes to position three.
